# Clean code & file size

- Keep each source file at **most 200 lines**. If a file approaches or exceeds that, split by responsibility (components, hooks, API helpers, styles, types).
- Prefer small, focused modules with a single clear purpose.
- Avoid deep nesting; extract early returns and named helpers.
- Do not add comments that only restate the code.
- Reuse existing patterns (`authApi`, `apiRequest`, `AuthLayout`, i18n keys) instead of duplicating logic.
- When editing a large file, leave it smaller or no bigger than before unless the task truly requires growth — then split.
